1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,300
What if you could query a ten-million-line codebase by meaning,
not keywords?

2
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:15,000
Derive intent across four languages, deterministically,
without AI hallucination.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
One behavior. Four surface syntaxes.
The human intent stays the same.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Keep what matters. Transform it. Combine the result.
Syntax is noise. Zero finds the signal.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:40,200
Each adapter lowers source into a universal Semantic Graph.

6
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:52,000
After that point, Zero sees no language-specific types or syntax.
It only sees intent.

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:03,400
Zero does not use AI at runtime.
Facts and fixed rules evaluate hypotheses.

8
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:18,000
This function has an inspectable proof:
Filter, Mapper, Reducer.

9
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:31,600
A compiler says only “type mismatch.”
Zero sees an accumulator inside a reduction loop.

10
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:44,000
The suggested fix is tied to the broken semantic role.

11
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:55,600
Same graph. Same evidence. Same answer.
The report is byte-stable.

12
00:01:55,600 --> 00:02:06,000
32 patterns are verified across four language transports.
Reasoning averages under one millisecond on the current corpus.

13
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:19,400
Codex and GPT-5.6 accelerated the Rust engine,
four adapters, and the verification suite.

14
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:31,000
Every conclusion remains inspectable, rules-based code.

15
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Ask for “filter then reduce.”
Zero matches cached semantic reports without reparsing source.

16
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Code should be searched by what it does.
This is Zero.
